  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Northwest Austin Municipal Utility District (Appellant)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7d911784d986-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Northwest Austin Municipal Utility District (Appellant), according to Northwest Austin Municipal Utility District (Appellant), the appellant argues that after more than 20\u202fyears of steadfast compliance with the Voting Rights Act, the district should be free from the intrusive burdens of preclearance and qualifies as a political subdivision eligible for a bailout."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Coleman",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7d911784d986-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The appellant points to data showing that, with respect to both Black and Hispanic voters, the record in covered jurisdictions is above the national average."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Coleman",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7d911784d986-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The appellant also notes that in Massachusetts the white\u2011Black voter registration and turnout differential is in the high\u201120s, far exceeding any covered jurisdiction."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Coleman",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7d911784d986-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Coleman, using modern data, the appellant argues that no state would be covered under the bailout formula, making the criteria outdated."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7d911784d986-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Katyal, the appellant contends that Section\u202f5 is working well and provides a deterrent against discriminatory voting practices."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7d911784d986-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Katyal, after 16,000 pages of testimony and 21 hearings, Congress concluded that its work on the issue was not finished."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Gregory S. Coleman",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7d911784d986-0003-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 63,
              "start": 63
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "7d911784d986303b3f6041f9306619afee5efae5cb0bd5f36fbda4cd48545055",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-7d911784d986-0003-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 64,
              "start": 64
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Gregory S. Coleman, the appellant argues that the facial challenge to the bailout provision is unconstitutional because Congress relied on outdated coverage criteria from the 1960s\u20111970s without updating them."
      }
    ],
